git show --remerge-diff needs git 2.36 or later: the option first
appears in Documentation/RelNotes/2.36.0.adoc of git.git.

The other option was a line in the fold recipes telling the agent to run
git show --remerge-diff itself. A WARN from prep is harder to skip.

With rerere on, a recorded resolution may still replay, but the WARN
stays: rerere does not bring back edits the merge made of its own.

Tested in scratch repos: a clean merge gets no WARN; a merge with a
conflict resolved by hand and a merge with an extra file added in it
each get the WARN, and the remerge-diff it names shows the conflict
markers next to the resolution.
